        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 rounded-2xl p-8 text-gray-200">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="mb-4">
            For a driveway, a patio or a garage slab where you want protection without maintenance, a silane-siloxane penetrating sealer is the right answer. Seven to ten years of service, nothing to strip, nothing to peel, and no change in how the concrete looks.
          </p>
          <p class="m-0">
            Choose a topical sealer instead only when appearance is the point — a wet look on pavers, a decorative stained floor, a polished interior slab. Those are legitimate reasons, but they come with a reapplication cycle that penetrating chemistry avoids entirely.
          </p>
        </div>

